Lines 49-55:
  BEFORE: Ethical subjectivists say that ‘x is right’ is a statement about someone’s attitude towards x. Here are three common versions of subjectivism:

Individual Subjectivism: $x$ is right $= I$ (the speaker) approve of $x$.

Cultural Relativism: $x$ is right = Society approves of $x$.

Divine Command Theory: $x$ is right = God approves of $x$.
  AFTER:  Ethical subjectivists say that ‘x is right’ is a statement about someone’s attitude towards x. Here are three common versions of subjectivism:

Individual Subjectivism: $x$ is right $= I$ (the speaker) approve of $x$.

Cultural Relativism: $x$ is right = Society approves of $x$.

Divine Command Theory: $x$ is right = God approves of $x$.
